[URL='https://mcdashboard.org/en/docs/server/installation/'][IMG]https://mcdashboard.org/assets/store/btn-install.png[/IMG][/URL][URL='https://mcdashboard.org/en/docs/'][IMG]https://mcdashboard.org/assets/store/btn-docs.png?v=1[/IMG][/URL][URL='https://mcdashboard.org/en/pricing/'][IMG]https://mcdashboard.org/assets/store/btn-pricing.png[/IMG][/URL]

[B]For support: [EMAIL]support@mcdashboard.org[/EMAIL][/B][/CENTER]

[SIZE=6][B]Your server, in every player's pocket.[/B][/SIZE]
[SIZE=5][I]Not another admin panel. A [B]live dashboard[/B] for the people who actually play on your server, built from the placeholders you already have.[/I][/SIZE]

[SIZE=5]MCDashboard is a free plugin that turns PlaceholderAPI into a dashboard on [B]Android and iOS[/B]. Players see their stats, your world and your server health in an app that needs no account and has no ads or third-party analytics. Anonymous usage statistics help us improve it and can be turned off; child mode never sends them. You decide what is visible, one placeholder at a time, and nothing is exposed until you turn it on. [B]Every number, table, chart and picture on a dashboard is one of those placeholders[/B]; there is no separate content system.[/SIZE]

[CENTER][IMG]https://mcdashboard.org/assets/store/app.png[/IMG][/CENTER]

[IMG]https://mcdashboard.org/assets/store/sec-features.png[/IMG]
[SIZE=5]Everything your server already tracks, in a dashboard people want to open. Every tile below is a placeholder you chose to expose.[/SIZE]

[IMG]https://mcdashboard.org/assets/store/ic-live.png?v=3[/IMG] [B][SIZE=6]Live, not refreshed.[/SIZE][/B]
[SIZE=5]Values arrive the moment they change, over a live connection. Polling is only the fallback when that connection is not available.[/SIZE]

[IMG]https://mcdashboard.org/assets/store/ic-shield.png?v=3[/IMG] [B][SIZE=6]Only what you allow.[/SIZE][/B]
[SIZE=5]The app asks for a placeholder by id. Arbitrary text is never evaluated, and a player's values stay private to their own device. The plugin is open source, so you can audit that instead of taking our word for it.[/SIZE]

[IMG]https://mcdashboard.org/assets/store/ic-lock.png?v=3[/IMG] [B][SIZE=6]HTTPS and pairing, built in.[/SIZE][/B]
[SIZE=5]The plugin serves HTTPS itself, with a certificate it generates or your own. Players pair with a five-minute code or a QR map, and you can cut a device off instantly.[/SIZE]

[IMG]https://mcdashboard.org/assets/store/ic-chart.png?v=3[/IMG] [B][SIZE=6]Charts that survive a restart.[/SIZE][/B]
[SIZE=5]Keep history in memory, or in SQLite, MySQL, MariaDB or PostgreSQL. From a couple of hours to a year of graphs, ready to query with SQL if you want to build on it.[/SIZE]

[IMG]https://mcdashboard.org/assets/store/ic-widgets.png?v=3[/IMG] [B][SIZE=6]Every widget. Every style. Free.[/SIZE][/B]
[SIZE=5]Gauges, rings, graphs, heatmaps, lists, leaderboards, player heads, images and more, in nine dashboard styles and seven accents. A LIST placeholder returns the rows for a leaderboard; an IMAGE placeholder is a picture or a map. The limits are on how many dashboards you make, never on how they look.[/SIZE]

[IMG]https://mcdashboard.org/assets/store/ic-map.png?v=3[/IMG] [B][SIZE=6]Your world, on the dashboard.[/SIZE][/B]
[SIZE=5]A map is an IMAGE placeholder: map:dynmap, map:squaremap, map:pl3xmap or map:bluemap, or any HTTPS image. The app draws it like any other picture tile, so the world around the player, your logo and an event banner are all the same mechanism.[/SIZE]

[IMG]https://mcdashboard.org/assets/store/ic-layout.png?v=3[/IMG] [B][SIZE=6]Dashboards on your terms.[/SIZE][/B]
[SIZE=5]One YAML file per board, a permission taken from its file name, a four-column grid, backgrounds and translations. Or design it on your phone in developer mode.[/SIZE]

[IMG]https://mcdashboard.org/assets/store/ic-network.png?v=3[/IMG] [B][SIZE=6]A network, not a pile of servers.[/SIZE][/B]
[SIZE=5]The Velocity and BungeeCord jars put one dashboard on the whole proxy. On Bedrock, PowerNukkitX runs the same plugin and the same app.[/SIZE]

[SIZE=3][I]Java 17, Spigot or Paper 1.18+, PlaceholderAPI. No other libraries: the HTTP server, the live feed and the JSON are the JDK's own.[/I][/SIZE]

[IMG]https://mcdashboard.org/assets/store/sec-app.png[/IMG]
[SIZE=5]The app is free on [B]Android and iOS[/B], needs no account, and follows your phone's light or dark mode and language (English, Dutch, French, German, Spanish).

Add a server, run [B]/mcdashboard link[/B] in game and enter the code (or scan the QR map). The app finds the server while you type, shows its name, MOTD and player count, and remembers the certificate you trusted. From then on its dashboards are tabs: the presets you publish and [B]My dashboard[/B] for tiles of their own. A server without the plugin can be added too: the app shows its icon, MOTD and players, warns that dashboards need the plugin, and offers a ready-made message with mcdashboard.org to send to the owner. When the plugin appears, one tap turns that entry into a normal server.

Tap a tile for its value, unit, range and chart period. One glance tells you whether it is live, polling or offline; when the signal drops, the last values stay, with their age. Players can drag, resize and preview their own tiles without touching the server's presets.[/SIZE]

[SIZE=5][B]Widgets[/B] put a card, or a whole dashboard, on the home screen. [B]Notifications[/B] watch a value and warn when it crosses a line, with six operators and a cooldown so a flapping value does not become a stream of alerts. Both are part of the paid side: the app unlock gives them on every server, a licensed server gives them to all of its players. An app lock, a backup of servers and dashboards, and an age mode for younger players are free.[/SIZE]

[CENTER][IMG]https://mcdashboard.org/assets/store/widgets.png[/IMG][/CENTER]

[SIZE=5][B]The world tab[/B] is not a separate map integration: it is an IMAGE placeholder. Point it at dynmap, squaremap, Pl3xMap or BlueMap, or at any picture, and it appears next to the stats like any other tile. It looks like this.[/SIZE]

[CENTER][IMG]https://mcdashboard.org/assets/store/map.png[/IMG][/CENTER]

[IMG]https://mcdashboard.org/assets/store/sec-pricing.png[/IMG]
[SIZE=5]Start free. Stay free if that is enough. There are two paid options, for two different people: the person holding the phone, and the person running the server.[/SIZE]

