[SIZE=5][B]Running the server?[/B] The server licence is the one that changes something for your community. [B]Just playing?[/B] The app unlock follows you to every server you join. If you have both, nothing changes: you already have everything.

Prices include VAT. Cancel any time. Nothing is deleted when a licence ends: extra dashboards and tiles stay visible as locked cards, and the longer history comes back with the licence.[/SIZE]

[IMG]https://mcdashboard.org/assets/store/sec-install.png[/IMG]
[SIZE=5]Four steps, and the security is as strict as you want it to be.[/SIZE]

[SIZE=5][B]1.[/B] [B]Install[/B] [URL='https://www.spigotmc.org/resources/placeholderapi.6245/']PlaceholderAPI[/URL] and the expansions you want to show, then put [B]MCDashboard.jar[/B] in [I]plugins/[/I].[/SIZE]

[SIZE=5][B]2.[/B] [B]Start the server once[/B], open [I]plugins/MCDashboard/config.yml[/I] and set [I]server.enabled: true[/I]. Choose the certificate: self-signed, your own, or TLS off behind a reverse proxy.[/SIZE]

[SIZE=5][B]3.[/B] [B]Choose what is visible[/B] in [I]placeholders.yml[/I], and arrange the preset dashboards in [I]dashboards/[/I]. A placeholder can be PUBLIC (anyone with the address) or PLAYER (only the paired player), and can require a permission.[/SIZE]

[SIZE=5][B]4.[/B] [B]Run [I]/mcdashboard link[/I][/B], open the app, add the server and enter the code. [I]/mcdashboard devices[/I] lists the paired devices; [I]/mcdashboard revoke <id>[/I] cuts one off immediately.[/SIZE]

[SIZE=5][B]Required:[/B] Java 17 and Spigot or Paper 1.18+, with PlaceholderAPI. [B]Bedrock:[/B] PowerNukkitX 3 and Java 21, with the PlaceholderAPI for PowerNukkitX. [B]Networks:[/B] Velocity 3.x or BungeeCord/Waterfall, Java 17, no PlaceholderAPI needed.

By default every player pairs before they see anything ([I]security.require-authentication[/I]). Public values can be read without pairing if you turn that off, and per-player values stay private to that player's device. Rate limits, client verification and background updates are in the security guide.[/SIZE]

[CENTER][IMG]https://mcdashboard.org/assets/store/add-server.png[/IMG][/CENTER]

[IMG]https://mcdashboard.org/assets/store/sec-about.png[/IMG]
[SIZE=5]Hi, I'm Maxim. I have been making Minecraft plugins for more than 13 years, including FeatherBoard. The idea goes back to [URL='https://www.spigotmc.org/resources/mcplaceholderdashboard-legacy.16351/']MCPlaceholderDashboard[/URL], a project I released in 2015 that never stopped sparking my interest. The first MCDashboard prototypes followed in 2020, built for private servers that wanted a scoreboard outside the game. That is still the idea: players see their own progress and their favourite server without an admin panel in the middle, and owners publish exactly the information they choose, and nothing else.

The plugin is open source under the AGPL-3.0, primarily so you can audit what runs on your server and verify that nothing leaves it that you did not allow. The app and the licence service are run by my company, [URL='https://mvdw-software.com']MVdW-Software[/URL]. You can read more about me on [URL='https://maximvdw.be/about']my website[/URL].

The plugin is free to download and free to use. The app is free too. The paid options exist to cover the servers, the app stores and the years of maintenance behind them, and they are listed above without small print.[/SIZE]

